<p style="margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;font-size:15px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,serif;color:black;border:none;line-height:14.0pt;"><span style="font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times&quot;,serif;color:#1C1E29;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;font-size:15px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,serif;color:black;border:none;line-height:14.0pt;"><span style="font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times&quot;,serif;color:#1C1E29;">Now what this does is instantly develop an ounce of trust in your mind for the company whose blog it is. How do they benefit from it? Well, they start with talking about the query and end up by showcasing how best to solve it and most often that happens with a product that they are dealing with.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;font-size:15px;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,serif;color:black;border:none;line-height:14.0pt;"><span style="font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Times&quot;,serif;color:#1C1E29;">&nbsp;</span></p>
